## Delivered: `ExportStatusWidget` native Apple surface (P4 · 0049)

A production-quality SwiftUI parity port of `web/.../ExportStatusWidget.tsx`, committed as `f3d5a370` (3 files, 1,387 insertions):

- **`apps/apple/Sources/Dashboard/Widgets/ExportStatusWidget.swift`** (955 lines) — registry metadata (`export-status`, 2×4/1×2/4×40), a pure framework-free reducer (merge + dedupe with admin-wins + status/recency sort + `fmtBytes`/`truncateFilename`), a `LoadableState`-mirroring feed + derived `ExportStatusViewState` machine, a P1/S8 provider seam (`ExportStatusProvider`/`ExportStatusFeedProvider` — the view does **no HTTP/KMP**), a P1/S11 `view.opened` telemetry seam, and the view with compact/standard/wide layouts + **all** loading/empty/error/stale/offline states using the real `TS*` component library.
- **`apps/apple/Tests/Unit/ExportStatusWidgetTests.swift`** (265 lines) — 23 tests: adapter, per-state machine, a11y-label builder, model/provider binding.

