## Honest gate caveat (environmental, documented in the log)
The end-to-end `xcodebuild build test` could **not** reach EXIT=0 in this sandbox — across 3 runs, **every** failure was a pre-existing UI-automation suite (`AppLaunchUITests`/`AuthOnboardingUITests`/`PushNotificationsUITests`), zero non-UI failures. Root cause is runner capability, not my code: global `xcode-select` is CommandLineTools (full Xcode present but un-selectable without sudo) plus shared-machine simulator contention; macOS `test` additionally needs a dev signing cert. I also had to map the prompt's nonexistent `TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets/` path onto the real XcodeGen source roots (`Sources/…`, `Tests/Unit/…`) so the surface actually compiles and is tested. All of this is recorded transparently in `p4-apple-dashboard-widgets-0049-ExportStatusWidget.log`.

